['The problem','Liquidation is automatic; determining whether a loss deserves compensation usually is not. A price mistake can transfer value from a solvent borrower before a protocol can respond.'],
['The supported policy','DemoLendingPool v1 only: 18-decimal collateral, 6-decimal USD-pegged test debt token, 80% liquidation threshold. A disputed price drop of at least 5% must be corroborated by a separate synthetic reference oracle staying within 1% of the pre-incident price. Each compensated borrower must be solvent before the deviation and liquidatable at the disputed price.'],
['Evidence collection','The controller validates the successful oracle transaction, reads the baseline at the preceding block, queries liquidation logs in a bounded incident window, and checks reconstructed borrower balances against the observed end state. Block hashes anchor the evidence. Fixtures cannot override these reads. Extra oracle updates, deposits, borrows, or repayments in the window require review.'],
['What the agent does','The controller collects evidence, retries failed reads with a bounded backoff, evaluates the restrictive policy, calculates losses, checks eligibility and produces a Merkle manifest. Optional LLM review can withhold approval but cannot override failed evidence checks. The default demo uses named deterministic rules and reports no model usage.'],
